<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirza Reza Kermani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1854–1896</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirza Reza Kermani was an Iranian radical, a follower of the pan-Islamist Jamal al-Din al-Afghani, who shot dead Naser al-Din Shah at the shrine of Shah Abdol-Azim near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tehran">Tehran</a> on 1 May 1896, on the eve of the shah's jubilee. He had earlier been imprisoned and tortured for his political activity, and was publicly hanged in Tehran in August 1896.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirza-reza-kermani.jpg" alt="Mirza Reza Kermani" width="320" height="473" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edward Granville Browne · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Persian_Revolution_of_1905-1909_(1910),_facing_p._62.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
